---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FeatureHero from "../components/FeatureHero.astro";
import PartnerLogos from "../components/PartnerLogos.astro";
import TwoColumnContent from "../components/TwoColumnContent.astro";
import ProfileLayout from "../components/ProfileLayout.astro";
import ProfileSocialCard from "../components/ProfileSocialCard.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import DrCronin from "../assets/images/img-Dr-Cronin-Eye-Laser-Surgeon-Brisbane.webp";
// import drCroninImage from "../assets/images/img-DrBrendanCroninOphthalmologi.jpg";
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import Schema from "../components/Schema.astro";
import { getProfilePageSchema } from "../utils/seo";

import drCroninImage from "../assets/images/dr-brendan-cronin-square.jpg";

const authorData = await getEntry("authors", "brendan-cronin");

const title = "Dr Brendan Cronin – Brisbane Corneal & Refractive Surgeon";
const description = `Dr. Brendan Cronin is a skilled ophthalmologist specializing in advanced eye care and surgery. Contact us today to book your eye health consultation!`;
const ogType = "website";
---

<BaseLayout
	title={title}
	showCurve={false}
	topColor="#ffffff"
	direction="down"
	bottomColor="transparent"
	description={description}
	ogType={ogType}
>
	<Fragment slot="head-schema">
		{
			authorData && (
				<Schema
					item={getProfilePageSchema(
						"/about-dr-brendan-cronin",
						authorData,
					)}
				/>
			)
		}
	</Fragment>
	<FeatureHero textPosition="center" textColor="light" bottomColor="#FFFFFF">
		<h1>About Dr Brendan Cronin</h1>
	</FeatureHero>

	<ProfileLayout>
		<!-- 3. Place the image in the named "image" slot -->
		<div slot="image">
			<Image
				src={drCroninImage}
				alt="A professional headshot of Dr, Brendan Cronin"
			/>
			<ProfileSocialCard
				websiteUrl="https://drbrendancronin.com.au/"
				linkedinUrl="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brendan-cronin-301a776b/"
			/>
		</div>

		<!-- 4. Place all your text content in the default slot -->
		<h4>MBBS (Hons), DipOphthSci, B.Com, LLB, FRANZCO</h4>
		<h2>
			Dr Cronin is a Corneal & Anterior Segment Surgeon & the Director of
			Education at the Queensland Eye Institute in Brisbane Australia.
		</h2>

		<p>
			Dr Brendan Cronin is a Brisbane-based Corneal, Cataract and
			Refractive Surgeon known for his expertise in <strong
				>complex cataract surgery and advanced anterior segment disease</strong
			>. He is the co-founder of Focus Vision. He grew up on the Gold
			Coast and completed his medical and ophthalmic training in Brisbane
			at the University of Queensland where he graduated from medicine
			with honours. He completed his ophthalmic training in Brisbane and
			then further trained in his subspecialty of Corneal, Refractive and
			Anterior Segment Surgery at the prestigious <a
				href="https://mft.nhs.uk/royal-eye/"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">Manchester Royal Eye Hospital</a
			> in the United Kingdom.
		</p>

		<p>
			Dr Cronin is a registered specialist with the <a
				href="https://www.ahpra.gov.au"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Australian Health Practitioner Regulatory Agency</a
			> and is a member of The Royal Australian and New Zealand College of
			Ophthalmologists (<a
				href="https://www.ranzco.edu"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">RANZCO</a
			>), The <a
				href="https://www.asoeye.org"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">Australian Society of Ophthalmology</a
			>, The <a
				href="https://www.escrs.org"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>European Society of Cataract and Refractive Surgery</a
			>, <a
				href="https://ebaanz.org"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">The Cornea Society</a
			>, and is a founding fellow of the World College of Refractive
			Surgery and Visual Sciences.
		</p>

		<p>
			His practice is focused on patients who require more than routine
			care — including those with previous LASIK or laser vision
			correction, irregular or diseased corneas, keratoconus, and
			challenging cataracts where surgical precision and experience are
			critical to achieving optimal outcomes.
		</p>

		<p>
			While many surgeons perform cataract surgery, Dr Cronin is
			frequently involved in <strong
				>cases where standard approaches are not enough</strong
			>.
		</p>

		<h3>A referral centre for complex cataract surgery</h3>

		<p>
			Dr Cronin has developed a reputation for managing <strong
				>technically demanding cataract cases</strong
			>, including:
		</p>

		<ul>
			<li>
				Cataract surgery after LASIK, PRK and other refractive
				procedures
			</li>
			<li>Irregular corneas and keratoconus</li>
			<li>High astigmatism requiring toric and advanced lens planning</li>
			<li>
				Premium intraocular lens cases requiring precise refractive
				outcomes
			</li>
			<li>
				Difficult or high-risk cataracts referred for specialist care
			</li>
		</ul>

		<p>
			These cases require careful planning, advanced diagnostics, and a
			deep understanding of corneal optics — an area in which Dr Cronin
			has subspecialty expertise.
		</p>

		<h3>Precision refractive outcomes</h3>

		<p>
			For patients seeking independence from glasses, cataract surgery is
			no longer just about removing the cataract — it is a refractive
			procedure.
		</p>

		<p>
			Dr Cronin has a strong focus on <strong
				>refractive cataract surgery</strong
			>, using modern intraocular lens technology and detailed
			pre-operative analysis to optimise visual outcomes. This includes
			the use of toric, extended depth of focus (EDOF), and multifocal
			lenses where appropriate, with a tailored approach based on each
			patient's eye and visual goals.
		</p>

		<p>
			This is why Dr Cronin offers Ray-Tracing LASIK at Focus Vision – he
			demands the best technology and the best refractive outcomes for his
			patients.
		</p>

		<h3>Training, research and leadership</h3>

		<p>
			Dr Cronin trained in Brisbane and completed advanced fellowship
			training in Corneal, Refractive and Anterior Segment Surgery at the
			internationally recognised Manchester Royal Eye Hospital in the
			United Kingdom.
		</p>

		<p>
			He is Director of Education at the Queensland Eye Institute and is
			actively involved in teaching and training ophthalmologists. He has
			participated in over 20 international clinical trials and holds an
			international patent in corneal cross-linking technology. His work
			reflects a continued commitment to advancing surgical techniques and
			improving patient outcomes.
		</p>

		<h3>A surgeon's perspective — and a patient's</h3>

		<p>
			I have been the patient! I needed urgent eye surgery when I was a
			medical student. Thankfully the surgery went very well and I
			maintained excellent vision - thanks to modern ophthalmology!!
			That's why I became an ophthalmologist. I fell in love with the
			amazing technology and treatments we have available. But this means
			I know what it is like to be in your position.
		</p>

		<p>
			Even better - I have had laser eye surgery! Yes - I believe in the
			safety and efficacy of the procedure so much that I have had it
			myself.
		</p>
	</ProfileLayout>

	<TwoColumnContent
		imageSrc={DrCronin}
		imageAlt="Brendan Cronin laser refractive surgery"
		imagePosition="left"
		backgroundColor="#FFFFFF"
		stylePreset="Eggshell"
	>
		<h2>Areas of expertise</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Complex micro-incision cataract surgery (including post-LASIK
				and irregular corneas)
			</li>
			<li>Refractive cataract surgery and premium intraocular lenses</li>
			<li>Laser vision correction (LASIK, PRK, CLEAR, ICL)</li>
			<li>Pterygium and ocular surface surgery</li>
			<li>Implantable Collamer Lenses</li>
			<li>
				Keratoconus including <a href="/cairsplan">CAIRS</a> and advanced
				corneal collagen cross linking
			</li>
		</ul>

		<!-- You can add lists, buttons, etc. here -->
	</TwoColumnContent>

	<PartnerLogos />
</BaseLayout>
